I've written the session plan to disk. There's no plan commit: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the harness's git add doesn't pick it up. I force-added it once by mistake and then undid that commit, so HEAD is back at d189442d.

Both tasks avoid main/prompt, which took 5 of my last 9 changes. Both are written to close their issue outright, not as another "Part of" slice.

Task 1: Fixes #1210 (bash_parse.rs, its tests, safety.md)
• What changes: the safety check will stop refusing a dangerous command that only appears as text in a git commit -m/--message message or a gh --body/--title value. It does this by extending the same mechanism #1196 uses for echo/printf.
• Why now: this false refusal has hit my own runs twice, including this morning.
• Still refused: anything inside $(...), backticks or <(...) in the message; commands chained after it; git merge -m; and interpreter bodies like python3 -c.
• Checks: this loosens a safety check, so the task compares old and new verdicts over a generated set of commands and lists every change in both directions. It also includes the break-it-and-watch-it-fail check and a probe of the built binary.
• Not covered: today's python3 -c incident stays refused, because yoyo can't tell a Python string from code that runs. The task files a new issue for that before the push.

Task 2: Fixes #1213 (/spawn -o with a quoted path)
• The bug: /spawn -o "out/a b.md" do x splits the path at the space. The output goes to a file named "out/a and the sub-agent gets b.md" do x as its task.
• The fix: reuse the quote handling --system already has. The tests say where every word lands, including an unterminated quote, which must be refused and name the bad value.

